Two ships of the [[Royal Navy]] have been named '''HMS ''P38'''''.

* {{HMS|P38|1917}}, a [[P-class sloop|P-class patrol boat]] launched in 1917. Renamed HMS ''Spey'' on 11 December 1925 and assigned to fishery protection, the vessel was sold in May 1938.
* {{HMS|P38|1941}}, a [[British U-class submarine|U-class submarine]] launched in July 1941 and sunk on 23 February 1942 by the Italian [[torpedo boat]] [[Italian torpedo boat Circe|''Circe'']] north of [[Tripoli, Libya]].

